  "brief": "Samsung is in talks to acquire data center cooling firm Modine for a rumored $5.6 billion, while a potential Tesla-SpaceX merger is reportedly worth $500 billion.\n\nSamsung / Modine (Rumored): Samsung and Modine Deal Rumors. Samsung is in talks to acquire data center cooling firm Modine [1, 2, 3]. The deal is rumored to be worth $5.6 billion [1]. Modine's stock surged over 25% pre-market after the news [3]. No terms have been disclosed yet [4].\nSpaceX / Tesla (Rumored): SpaceX and Tesla Merger Talks. SpaceX and Tesla are in merger talks with an announcement possible in December [9, 10]. SpaceX could announce a $1.5 trillion Tesla merger in December [11]. There is an 80%-90% chance of a Tesla-SpaceX merger, with a $500 price tag [12]. A $2T bid has been made for a SpaceX-Tesla merger, drawing a Reuters warning [13].\nTensor / RAIN (Announced): Tensor to Take 90% of RAIN. Tensor is acquiring 90% of RAIN in a reverse merger [17, 18]. The deal is a strategic business combination between the two companies [17, 18]. No further information is available on the deal at this stage [17, 18].\nHancock Whitney / Trustmark (Announced): Hancock Whitney to Buy Trustmark. Hancock Whitney is buying Trustmark in a $3.2B deal [19, 20, 21]. The deal is set to be completed in early 2027 [23]. The companies have announced the merger agreement [22, 23].\nArdent Health / Boone Health (Announced): Ardent Health to Acquire Boone Health. Ardent Health is acquiring Boone Health [24, 25]. The deal has been announced [24, 25]. No further information is available [24, 25].\nRed Sox / Jake Bauers (Announced): Red Sox and Jake Bauers. The Red Sox have agreed to a 4-year, $58 million deal with 1B Jake Bauers [26]. The deal is part of a larger agreement that includes a stake in Cadillac F1 [27]. No further details have been announced [27].\nEP Group / Fnac Darty (Announced): EP Group to Acquire Fnac Darty. EP Group is acquiring Fnac Darty [28, 29]. The takeover bid was initiated by EP Group [28]. The closing date of the tender offer is November 9, 2026 [29].\nHall Chadwick Acquisition Corp / REEcycle Holdings, Inc. (Announced): Hall Chadwick Acquisition Corp to Acquire REEcycle Holdings. Hall Chadwick Acquisition Corp and REEcycle Holdings, Inc. are acquiring each other [30]. The deal was announced [30]. No further information is available [30].\n\nAlso worth knowing:\n- The Real Economy Blog, Nov 13 12:33 PM ET: 5 things to know in life sciences: Week of Nov. 9, 2026 [31].\n- The Globe and Mail, Nov 13 11:52 AM ET: H&R unitholders vote against GO REIT takeover bid [32].\n- 24/7 Wall St., Nov 13 10:53 AM ET: United’s CEO Says He’s “100%” Sure an American Deal Could Be Approved [33].",
